 | 0168 | 2026-10-18 | Cash drawer, your urgent request: **the drawer is now one shared drawer for the shop and its status syncs between registers.** Until now a register's drawer (the shift and the notes-and-coins ledger) never left the device. A change is still written locally first, exactly as before, so the drawer keeps working offline, and is then uploaded to the same `pos_settings` metaobject the shared settings and scanner calibration use (handle `drawer`, versioned like them); the 25-second poll in `App.tsx` picks up another register's copy. A push folds in any ledger entries another register wrote before it writes, so a cash sale on one iPad is never overwritten by the other: entries are merged by id and the counts move by the deltas we had not seen. The shift (open/closed, float, paid in and out) is last-write-wins by version, but a push that only changed the ledger follows a newer shift from the other register, so a sale here cannot revert a drawer just opened there. **Expected cash now counts every register's cash since the drawer opened**, not just this one, because there is one physical drawer. New `src/lib/drawerSync.ts` (pure: which entries are new to us, and the merged ledger), tests `tests/drawersync.test.ts` (10). `drawerChanged()` in `src/lib/sync.ts` marks and uploads a change, called from the drawer screen (open, paid in/out, correct contents, close), swap, daily banking, a cash refund and a cash sale. Practice mode never sends, like everything else behind the training guard. **Decided without you, change any you disagree with:** one shared drawer (you chose this), so two registers opening at once is last-one-wins; the sync carries the drawer's state only, not a copy per register. **Worth knowing:** a register that already had a local drawer keeps it until something changes it, and the first register to change the drawer after this update creates the shared copy. Not tried on a real iPad. | your urgent request |
